<figure class="authority" data-r21-authority aria-labelledby="r21-authority-title">
 <figcaption id="r21-authority-title"><span>Figure 1</span> Moving the route does not close an old connection</figcaption>
 <fieldset><legend>Transfer protocol</legend><label><input type="radio" name="r21-protocol" value="unsafe" checked /> Change route and promote</label><label><input type="radio" name="r21-protocol" value="fenced" /> Enforce old-primary fence first</label></fieldset>
 <div class="route"><b>New connections</b><span data-route data-live>Old primary</span></div>
 <div class="servers"><div><b>Old primary</b><p data-old data-live>Writer</p><small>A client already has this connection</small></div><div><b>Candidate</b><p data-new data-live>Read-only standby</p><small>Has its own replayed history</small></div></div>
 <div class="attempt"><b>Existing client's write</b><span data-attempt data-live>Not attempted</span></div>
 <p data-explanation data-live aria-live="polite">There is one writer. A client already connected to it will not consult DNS again for every SQL command.</p>
 <div class="controls" role="group" aria-label="Write authority transfer steps"><button type="button" data-play>Play</button><button type="button" data-back>Back</button><button type="button" data-next>Next</button><button type="button" data-reset>Reset</button><span data-step>1 / 5</span><div data-hold><span></span></div></div>
 <details><summary>Both protocols as text</summary><p>The controller suspects the old primary because it cannot reach it. Changing routing and promoting the candidate can leave both servers writable. An existing client can still write to the old primary, creating a second history. With an enforced fence, the old primary loses write ability before the candidate gains authority; the old connection cannot keep writing. Candidate history acceptance is a separate requirement in both cases.</p></details>
 <p class="caption">Conceptual partition: the controller loses contact with the old primary while an existing client can still reach it. No network partition was injected in the native test; that test promotes an owned standby with its old primary deliberately alive.</p>
</figure>
<style>
figure{font-family:var(--font-sans)}figcaption{font-family:var(--font-serif)}

.authority{margin:2rem 0}.authority figcaption{font-size:1.12rem;margin-bottom:.8rem}.authority figcaption span{font:.75rem var(--font-mono);text-transform:uppercase;margin-right:.6rem}.authority fieldset{border:1px solid var(--color-rule);padding:.8rem;display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:.5rem}.authority legend{font-size:.8rem}.authority label{display:flex;gap:.35rem;align-items:center;padding:.3rem;font-size:.85rem}.route,.attempt{display:flex;justify-content:space-between;gap:1rem;padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule);font-size:.85rem}.servers{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr;gap:1rem;padding:1rem;background:var(--color-surface);border:1px solid var(--color-rule)}.servers>div{border:2px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.8rem}.servers p{font-size:1rem;min-height:3rem;margin:.6rem 0}.servers small{display:block;font-size:.75rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}.authority>[data-explanation]{min-height:6rem;border-left:3px solid var(--color-accent);padding:.5rem .8rem}.controls{display:flex;gap:.5rem;flex-wrap:wrap;background:var(--color-surface);padding:.8rem;border:1px solid var(--color-rule)}.controls button{font:inherit;background:var(--color-surface);color:var(--color-text);border:1px solid var(--color-text-secondary);padding:.4rem .7rem;cursor:pointer}.controls button:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--color-accent);outline-offset:2px}.controls [aria-disabled=true]{opacity:.55}[data-step]{margin-left:auto;align-self:center;font:.8rem var(--font-mono)}[data-hold]{height:3px;flex-basis:100%;background:var(--color-rule)}[data-hold] span{display:block;height:100%;width:0;background:var(--color-accent)}.caption{font-size:.85rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary)}details{margin:.8rem 0}summary{cursor:pointer}@media(max-width:500px){.servers{padding:.6rem;gap:.6rem}.servers>div{padding:.6rem}.route,.attempt{display:grid;gap:.35rem}.authority>[data-explanation]{min-height:9rem}}
</style>
<script>
import {stepper} from '../../figures/stepper.mjs';
document.querySelectorAll('[data-r21-authority]').forEach(root=>{
 let fenced=false;const q=(s:string)=>root.querySelector(s) as HTMLElement;
 const player=stepper(root,{steps:()=>5,draw(s:number){
 q('[data-route]').textContent=s<3?'Old primary':'Candidate';q('[data-old]').textContent=fenced&&s>=2?'Fenced · cannot write':s===1?'Still writer · controller cannot reach it':'Writer';q('[data-new]').textContent=s>=3?'Promoted writer':'Read-only standby';q('[data-attempt]').textContent=s<4?'Not attempted':fenced?'Refused by enforced fence':'Accepted on old primary';
 const text=['There is one writer. A client already connected to it will not consult DNS again for every SQL command.','The controller misses the old primary. That is evidence of lost contact, not proof that every client has lost contact or that the server stopped.',fenced?'The controller establishes and verifies a fence. The old authority cannot keep writing, including through an existing connection.':'The controller proceeds without an enforced fence. The old server can still accept an existing client even if new connections will use another route.', 'The candidate is promoted and the route changes. '+(fenced?'There is now one permitted writer. Its history must still pass acceptance.':'Both servers can now write. Changing a route did not revoke the old server’s authority.'),fenced?'The old connection cannot write. Reconcile the candidate history, then restore redundancy while keeping the former primary from restarting as a writer.':'The old connection commits more work to a different history. A later restart or route change does not merge those histories.'];q('[data-explanation]').textContent=text[s];
 }});
 root.querySelectorAll('input').forEach(el=>el.addEventListener('change',()=>{fenced=(el as HTMLInputElement).value==='fenced';player.render();}));
});
</script>
